  "notes": "Fighting clause (36:26-31): not glossed; the verse's own «كما يقاتلونكم كافة» keeps its reciprocity; As-Sa'di's discussion of abrogation is not used. 36:22-25: As-Sa'di leaves «فيهن» open (the twelve or the four), so the neutral «فلتحذروا من ظلم أنفسكم فيها» is used. A moon for the months, stars for the heavens, geometric for «أربعة حرم», light for «مع المتقين». STAGING v4: Stays ambient (the months as Allah decreed them, with a fighting clause); nobody is drawn. Night sky: a moon for the months (36:2), stars for the heavens (36:13), a second moon for the four sacred months (36:17; geometric is kept for the Names), a geometric plate on the Name for Allah being with the pious (36:34). The background stays quiet on 36:9-15 (His decree, the day He created the heavens and the earth) and on the fighting clause 36:26-31."
